    "result_text": "All 54 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rule with a points system across two files:\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (the DTOs are generated from this spec) \u2014 added a new `membershipPoints` property to the `Owner` schema and rewrote the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the points-band mapping.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints` and split the computation into two methods:\n\n- `membershipPoints(owner)`: starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, `+3` when tenure (days from `registrationDate` to today) exceeds 365.\n- `membershipLevel(owner)`: maps points \u2192 level: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\nBoth fields are now returned. The `AuditOwnerCreated` log still reads `membershipLevel` and works unchanged.\n\nVerification against the spec's worked cases (all green): a fresh owner with email + no namesake = 3 points \u2192 level 2 (Cp15/Cp24/Cp40); the third household member with email = 5 points (2+1+2) \u2192 level 3 (Cp23); and a new owner maxed on non-tenure factors caps at 5 points \u2192 level 3, never 4, since only tenure (+3) reaches 6 (Cp39).",
