    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands. The endpoint is wired in `api/owners.POST.yml` as a 17-step pipeline; every step from `checkIdentityUnique` onward runs inside a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), so all the reads below see one consistent view and the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (handled by the `AuthorizationDeniedException` escalation) and nothing below runs.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (validation + normalization side-effects)\n\nBinds the `@RequestBody` once, republishes it, and on any failure throws `OwnerFieldsValidationException` \u2192 **400** with an `errors` array naming each bad field. In this order:\n\n1. **firstName** required (non-null, non-blank).\n2. **lastName** required.\n3. **address**: normalized to canonical form (mutates the request); if blank *after* normalization \u2192 `address` error.\n4. **city** required.\n5. **telephone** required.\n6. **telephone normalization \u2192 E.164** (mutates the request): strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+` and its country code, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; total must be 8\u201315 digits; `+61` must have 9 national digits, `+1` must have 10. Invalid \u2192 `telephone` error. (Skipped if telephone was blank.)\n7. **email normalization** (via `OwnerEmail.normalize`, mutates the request; can add an `email` error).\n8. **postcode** (optional): if present must be exactly 4 digits, and for a known city-region (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range; otherwise \u2192 `postcode` error. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode.\n9. **registrationDate** (optional): if present, must not be after the server's current date (no future-dating) \u2192 else `registrationDate` error.\n\n## Steps 2\u20134 \u2014 hard-duplicate / capacity gates (reads inside the transaction)\n\n10. **`CheckIdentityUnique`** \u2014 scans all owners; if one has the *same normalized telephone AND same lower-cased email*, throws `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409** (identityKey = `telephone|email|householdId`). Note: telephone is part of identity, so same-household owners with different phones do *not* collide.\n11. **`CheckHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 bypassed if the request set `sharesHousehold`, or if postcode is missing. Otherwise computes `householdId` (normalized lastName + postcode) and if any existing owner shares it, throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` \u2192 **409**.\n12. **`CheckCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50, throws `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n\n13. Maps the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` to a new `Owner` entity (via `OwnerMapper`).\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `DefaultRegistrationDate` (mutates entity)\n\n14. If no date supplied, uses the server's current date; then rolls any Saturday/Sunday **forward to the next Monday** so the persisted `registrationDate` is always a business day.\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `CheckDailyLimit`\n\n15. Counts owners already registered on the (adjusted) registrationDate; if \u2265 100, throws `DailyLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## Steps 8\u201313 \u2014 derived-field assignments (mutate the entity; all read within the transaction, before save)\n\n16. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`: REGION from postcode\u2192city\u2192`UNKNOWN`, HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName). Pure function, no repo read.\n17. **`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 sets `householdId` from normalized lastName + postcode.\n18. **`AssignHouseholdMemberCount`** \u2014 counts persisted owners sharing that `householdId`, **plus 1** for this new owner (household size after this create).\n19. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 counts existing owners with same firstName + lastName (case-insensitive), excluding this new one.\n20. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when **more than 80** owners were already registered on this registrationDate.\n21. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate = false` by default; skipped (left false) if `sharesHousehold` or no postcode; otherwise if an existing owner shares lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but has a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <that owner's id>`.\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n\n22. **Persists** the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (generates the id).\n\n## Step 15 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n\n23. **Side-effect (logging):** emits an `AUDIT` logger line with `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and derived `membershipLevel`.\n\n## Step 16 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n\n24. Maps the entity to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. Transaction commits.\n\n**A couple of notes worth flagging:**\n- The comments describe a 17-step pipeline but there are effectively these gates plus assignments; every read-based check (identity, household, city, daily limit, member/namesake counts) uses `ownerRepository.findAll()` and counts only already-persisted owners \u2014 correct only because they all share the one write transaction.\n- Beyond `ValidateOwnerFields`, a `DataIntegrityViolationException` at save also has an escalation handler, so a DB-constraint violation is handled there rather than in the pipeline."
